:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ADDENVVAR.Add Environment Variable (ADDENVVAR)
:P.Use the Add Environment Variable (ADDENVVAR) command to add an
environment variable to the job or the system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDENVVAR/ENVVAR'.Environment variable (ENVVAR)
:P.The name of the environment variable.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDENVVAR/VALUE'.Initial value (VALUE)
:P.The initial value for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NULL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDENVVAR/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDENVVAR/LEVEL'.Level (LEVEL)
:P.The level for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDENVVAR/REPLACE'.Replace existing entry (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGENVVAR.Change Environment Variable (CHGENVVAR)
:P.Use the Change Environment Variable (CHGENVVAR) command to change an
environment variable of the job or the system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGENVVAR/ENVVAR'.Environment variable (ENVVAR)
:P.The name of the environment variable.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGENVVAR/VALUE'.New value (VALUE)
:P.The new value for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NULL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGENVVAR/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGENVVAR/LEVEL'.Level (LEVEL)
:P.The level for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVENVVAR.Remove Environment Variable (RMVENVVAR)
:P.Use the Remove Environment Variable (RMVENVVAR) command to remove an
environment variable of the job or the system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVENVVAR/ENVVAR'.Environment variable (ENVVAR)
:P.The name of the environment variable.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVENVVAR/LEVEL'.Level (LEVEL)
:P.The level for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKENVVAR.Work with Environment Var (WRKENVVAR)
:P.Use the Work with Environment Var (WRKENVVAR) command to work with
the job's or the system's environment variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKENVVAR/LEVEL'.Level (LEVEL)
:P.The level for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
